WEBVTT

00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:30.476
EP: No, when you do both ends.

00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:33.226
It's not that it's complicated.
It's that it's both ends.

00:28:33.250 --> 00:28:35.518
Because I frankly don't think
that one can prove

00:28:35.542 --> 00:28:36.934
that it is this versus that.

00:28:36.958 --> 00:28:40.893
I think that it is a feedback loop.

00:28:40.917 --> 00:28:44.351
the more safe you feel,
the more risk you take,

00:28:44.375 --> 00:28:48.309
but also the more risk you take,
the more trusting you can be.

00:28:48.333 --> 00:28:50.101
AG: Sure, but as an experimentalist,

00:28:50.125 --> 00:28:53.101
I can ask, "OK, which is
the more important starting condition?

00:28:53.125 --> 00:28:55.268
And if you have a chicken
and the egg choice,

00:28:55.292 --> 00:28:57.934
do you want to start
with trust leading the risk-taking

00:28:57.958 --> 00:29:00.018
or is the effect stronger in reverse?"